{"units": [{"id": "thermaino-note1", "translation": "τῷδέ τἂν δολώματι πολλοὺς ἀναιρῶν πολλά θερμαίνοι φρενί [with this deceit, killing many, he would warm his heart greatly], where θερμαίνοι [would warm] is then so strangely said that it seems it should be left even to the interpolator who wrote these verses, who perhaps wrote θέρμ᾽ ἄνοι [hot things, open up], i.e. audacity or wickedness."}, {"id": "thermaino-quote1", "translation": "The sun's circle passed through the middle of its course, warming with its flame."}, {"id": "thermaino-word1", "translation": "with this deceit, killing many, he would warm his heart greatly"}, {"id": "thermaino-word2", "translation": "would warm"}, {"id": "thermaino-word3", "translation": "hot things, open up"}, {"id": "thermoergos-orth1", "translation": "hot-working"}, {"id": "thermoergos-def1", "translation": "See θερμός."}, {"id": "thermoergos-word1", "translation": "hot"}, {"id": "thermonous-orth1", "translation": "hot-minded"}, {"id": "thermonous-def1", "translation": "having a hot mind, inflamed"}, {"id": "thermonous-quote1", "translation": "But I, hot-minded, will quickly cast him into fetters."}, {"id": "thermos-orth1", "translation": "hot"}, {"id": "thermos-def1", "translation": "hot"}, {"id": "thermos-def2", "translation": "bold, wicked"}, {"id": "thermos-note1", "translation": "Thus Triclinius. θερμοεργῷ Μ [hot-working M] from a gloss."}, {"id": "thermos-quote1", "translation": "with hot bolts of unapproachable fire-breathing storm"}, {"id": "thermos-quote2", "translation": "cut with hot bloody offering"}, {"id": "thermos-quote3", "translation": "uttering harsh wintery ruin beneath a hot liver"}, {"id": "thermos-quote4", "translation": "hot baths"}, {"id": "thermos-quote5", "translation": "with hot streams of soft water"}, {"id": "thermos-quote6", "translation": "a pious man boarding a ship with hot sailors"}, {"id": "thermos-quote7", "translation": "the god laughs at a hot man"}, {"id": "thermos-word1", "translation": "hot-working M"}, {"id": "thermodon-orth1", "translation": "Thermodon"}, {"id": "thermodon-def1", "translation": "Thermodon, a river of Cappadocia"}, {"id": "thermodon-quote1", "translation": "who will one day inhabit Themiscyra around the Thermodon"}, {"id": "theros-orth1", "translation": "summer"}, {"id": "theros-def1", "translation": "summer"}, {"id": "theros-def2", "translation": "harvest"}, {"id": "theros-note1", "translation": "Figuratively"}, {"id": "theros-note2", "translation": "Thus Schuetzius corrected for ὁ ἔρως [love]."}, {"id": "theros-quote1", "translation": "a sure sign of fruitful summer"}, {"id": "theros-quote2", "translation": "those who bring winter and summer to mortals"}, {"id": "theros-quote3", "translation": "For hybris, flowering, produced a crop of ruin, from which it reaps a harvest of all tears"}, {"id": "theros-quote4", "translation": "but also to reap these many things, a wretched harvest"}, {"id": "theros-word1", "translation": "love"}, {"id": "thesmios-orth1", "translation": "lawful"}, {"id": "thesmios-def1", "translation": "lawful"}, {"id": "thesmios-def2", "translation": "θέσμιον [lawful thing] as substantive: law"}, {"id": "thesmios-quote1", "translation": "the doer must suffer; for it is lawful"}, {"id": "thesmios-quote2", "translation": "overthrows of new laws"}, {"id": "thesmios-quote3", "translation": "third this is written in the laws of most-honored Justice"}, {"id": "thesmios-word1", "translation": "lawful thing"}, {"id": "thesmos-orth1", "translation": "law"}, {"id": "thesmos-def1", "translation": "institution, law"}, {"id": "thesmos-def2", "translation": "of a musical mode, like νόμος [law, custom]"}, {"id": "thesmos-note1", "translation": "thus I corrected for χαρίζεσθαι [to gratify]"}, {"id": "thesmos-note2", "translation": "according to the scholiast who explains it as ὁ τοῦ ἡμετέρου ὕμνου νόμος [the law of our hymn]."}, {"id": "thesmos-quote1", "translation": "he urged the law that fire not be broken"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote2", "translation": "the law of fate given by the gods"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote3", "translation": "I will establish this law for all time"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote4", "translation": "to learn my laws"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote5", "translation": "I will tell you this great law of Athena"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote6", "translation": "you may now hear the law"}, {"id": "thesmos-quote7", "translation": "this kindly law does not neglect Cypris"}, {"id": "thesmos-word1", "translation": "to gratify"}, {"id": "thesmos-word2", "translation": "law, custom"}, {"id": "thesmos-word3", "translation": "the law of our hymn"}, {"id": "thespesios-orth1", "translation": "divinely speaking"}, {"id": "thespesios-def1", "translation": "divinely speaking"}, {"id": "thespesios-quote1", "translation": "from where do you have the boundaries of the divine path, ill-omened?"}, {"id": "thespizo-orth1", "translation": "to prophesy"}, {"id": "thespizo-def1", "translation": "to prophesy"}, {"id": "thespizo-quote1", "translation": "already I prophesied all sufferings to the citizens"}, {"id": "thespizo-quote2", "translation": "to us at least you seem to prophesy trustworthy things"}, {"id": "thespisma-orth1", "translation": "oracle"}, {"id": "thespisma-def1", "translation": "oracle"}, {"id": "thespisma-quote1", "translation": "Zeus sends oracles to Loxias"}, {"id": "thespiodeo-orth1", "translation": "to sing oracles, to prophesy"}, {"id": "thespiodeo-def1", "translation": "to sing oracles, to prophesy"}, {"id": "thespiodeo-quote1", "translation": "I am likely to prophesy soon"}, {"id": "thespiodos-orth1", "translation": "prophetic"}, {"id": "thespiodos-def1", "translation": "prophetic"}, {"id": "thespiodos-note1", "translation": "Thus Hermannus: θεσπιωδόν φόβον [prophetic fear] etc. M."}, {"id": "thespiodos-quote1", "translation": "many-worded prophetic arts"}, {"id": "thespiodos-word1", "translation": "prophetic fear"}, {"id": "thesprotos-orth1", "translation": "Thesprotus"}, {"id": "thesprotos-def1", "translation": "Thesprotus"}, {"id": "thesprotos-quote1", "translation": "Dodona, where there are oracles and the seat of Thesprotian Zeus"}, {"id": "thessalos-orth1", "translation": "Thessalus"}, {"id": "thessalos-def1", "translation": "Thessalus"}, {"id": "thessalos-quote1", "translation": "a city of the Thessalians"}, {"id": "thestias-orth1", "translation": "Thestias"}, {"id": "thestias-def1", "translation": "Thestias, daughter of Thestius (Althaea)"}, {"id": "thestias-quote1", "translation": "the wretched child-destroying Thestias"}, {"id": "thesphatelogos-orth1", "translation": "prophetic"}, {"id": "thesphatelogos-def1", "translation": "prophetic, prophesying"}, {"id": "thesphatelogos-note1", "translation": "A word not read elsewhere."}, {"id": "thesphatelogos-quote1", "translation": "faithful prophetic wife"}, {"id": "thesphaton-orth1", "translation": "oracle"}, {"id": "thesphaton-def1", "translation": "oracle, prophecy"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote1", "translation": "if there will be fruit according to the oracles of Loxias"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote2", "translation": "oracles are not blunted"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote3", "translation": "Zeus commanded the fulfillment of the oracles"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote4", "translation": "if one must trust the oracles of the gods"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote5", "translation": "I am at a loss with the dim-sighted oracles"}, {"id": "thesphaton-quote6", "translation": "the highest interpreter of oracles"}]}